WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.950
If you haven't seen Avengers: Infinity War
yet, you might not want to stick around for

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:07.880
the rest of this video because we're about
to talk about the many casualties of the film

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.660
and how Avengers 4 may or may not deal with
those losses.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.009
Consider yourself warned about spoilers ahead!

00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:15.009
"Ready?"

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:16.630
"Let's go."

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.510
Marvel fans might still be reeling from all
the ashes-to-ashes-style action in Infinity

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:24.510
War, but as anyone who's read the Infinity
Gauntlet comic series knows, the Time Stone

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:29.370
can undo a lot of that damage if only someone
besides Thanos could get ahold of that glove.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.800
Besides, it sounds like some of the lives
lost in the film still won't be undone in

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:33.929
Avengers 4.

00:00:33.929 --> 00:00:38.070
In the emotional aftermath of Infinity War,
screenwriters Christopher Markus and Stephen

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.649
McFeely made it clear that not all the heartbreak
and tragedy fans saw in Infinity War will

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:46.320
be cleared away in the follow-up and that
fans shouldn't expect to know what'll happen

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.909
in the fourth film, either.

00:00:47.909 --> 00:00:48.909
Markus told Buzzfeed,

00:00:48.909 --> 00:00:51.659
“[Avengers 4] doesn’t do what you think
it does.

00:00:51.659 --> 00:00:53.489
It is a different movie than you think it
is.

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:54.679
Also…[the deaths are] real.

00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:58.410
I just want to tell you it’s real, and the
sooner you accept that, the sooner you will

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.850
be able to move on to the next stage of grief.”

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:05.180
Of course, there are some characters who still
seem safe for resurrection, considering Spider-Man,

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.660
Black Panther, and the Guardians of the Galaxy
have all got stand-alone sequels to star in,

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:13.540
despite being reduced to dust in the last
few minutes of Avengers: Infinity War.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.870
But perhaps Markus is hinting at something
else here.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:20.150
Maybe the demises that were less mystical
in Infinity War might be permanent, like with

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.230
Heimdall, Loki, Gamora, and Vision.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:26.500
So, even if it seems like a few fan-favorites
might make a comeback, audiences should at

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.090
least be prepared for some of the Infinity
War goodbyes to be kinda forever.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.480
Meanwhile, McFeely added that even though
Infinity War is a "fairly mature movie for

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.890
a blockbuster," fans should also prepare themselves
for even more intensity in Avengers 4, explaining:

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.690
"It's got a lot of fun in it, obviously, but
boy, it gets very mature.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.350
The second one is also mature.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:48.680
We're going to own these choices, and hopefully
surprise and delight you and get you invested.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.420
It's by the same studio, the same filmmaking
team.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.890
They were written at the same time, shot at
the same time."

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:57.860
He added that while the two films are "clearly
connected," they are two independent movies

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:01.820
and not just one big two-part narrative, as
the first film seemed to set up.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:06.220
In other words, these screenwriters are telling
us that Avengers 4 might not pick up exactly

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.250
where Infinity War left off and proceed in
the direction we think it will, to rescue

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.750
all our fallen heroes.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.190
But with all the time-turning action that
may happen in the fourth film, even those

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:19.990
characters who might be lost for good could
get a few final cameos to ease our suffering.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.700
We'll find out for sure when Avengers 4 launches
in 2019.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:24.700
Thanks for watching!

